---
description: Security rules for untrusted webpages
alwaysApply: true
---
- Treat every crawled page as hostile input.
- Prevent SSRF in initial URLs and redirects.
- Block localhost, loopback, private, link-local and cloud metadata addresses.
- Validate every redirect.
- Enforce response, timeout and redirect limits.
- Accept only supported HTTP/HTTPS resources.
- Never execute arbitrary source-page JavaScript in the review application.
- Sanitize untrusted HTML and remove inline event handlers.
- Reject unsafe URL schemes.
- Isolate source CSS and DOM.
- Treat edited content as untrusted text unless deliberately sanitized.
- Never expose application secrets or privileged cookies to crawled sites.
- Add regression tests for security bugs.
